From e0ccb68a1d59c0693f53a35ad8c5b652696981cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:23:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/32] ww3d2, stage 2 milestone 1: Direct3D 8 headers; the
 Direct3D half of ww3d2 compiles

- xbox/include: d3d8.h, d3d8types.h, d3d8caps.h, d3dx8.h (+ d3dx8core/tex/math forwarders),
  with the DirectX 8 SDK's names and values; interfaces as C++ classes (implemented next, on
  pbkit). D3DX math (matrix product, transpose, Vec3Transform, FVF vertex size) implemented.
- xbox_win32_types.h: RECT, POINT, GUID, IUnknown, GDI handles, HIWORD/LOWORD...
- prelude also brings in those types and mmsystem.h, as windows.h does on PC
- dx8wrapper.h: Convert_Color / Clamp_Color without the stack-juggling inline asm on Xbox
  (same results: truncation, and the CMOV path's bit-level clamp incl. -0/inf/NaN)
- window management, desktop gamma, a dialog box and movie capture skipped on Xbox
- usual fixes, mostly automated: loop scoping (moved declarations), two-word casts,
  template<>, friend-only declaration, const strchr, false as a null pointer
